Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 1.8.8
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Builds one cell-type-specific Pando TF-peak-metabolic-gene candidate universe across conditions and fits a condition-balanced elastic-net multi-task regulatory model with a shared global backbone, condition deviations, and stability-selected condition sub-networks. Active condition target genes define complete-GPR core reactions and annotation-expanded biological meta-modules. Meta-modules are merged into one reaction catalogue without local FASTCORE completion. For each medium scenario, the package constructs one shared union GEM and performs a single global FASTCORE completion before directional COMPASS-like scoring. Integrated RNA support and shared-scale ATAC regulatory evidence are converted to reaction penalties. Pinned human and mouse GEMs are bundled for offline use, with platform-aware parallel execution and audited progress and timing output.
